{
 "encounter_id": "00847",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hi. I'm a runner. Skipped beats. Sometimes. It worries me."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How often do you notice them?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A few times a month. During recovery, after a run. Never during."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What does it feel like?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A thump. Then a pause. Then a big beat."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any dizziness, chest pain or fainting with it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. None of those."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How much do you run? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Forty miles a week. Training for a marathon. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any family history of heart problems or sudden death? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Not that I know of. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What do you take?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A tablet from the sports clinic, a small orange one, for iron, I think. I can't remember the name. I take it most days. Not every day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "So it's meant to be daily, you take it most days, and you can't name it. Any allergies?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "None."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any other health history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Asthma, as a child. And an ankle fracture, years ago."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you use caffeine, energy gels, or supplements? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Three coffees. And gels on long runs. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check your numbers. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Resting pulse 48, blood pressure 108 over 66, temperature 36.5, oxygen 99 percent.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My pulse is always low. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's what I'd expect for a distance runner. Let me listen to your heart.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Sure. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Slow and regular, with the odd extra beat, and no murmur."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What does that mean? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The skipped beats you describe are most likely ectopic beats, extra beats that are common in athletes and usually harmless."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Should I stop running? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "No. I'd like to confirm it, so I'd like to arrange an ECG today, and a 24-hour heart monitor."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Cut back on the coffee a bit, drink enough, and keep your salts up. Take the iron tablet with vitamin C, not with coffee."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If you ever get chest pain, faint, or the palpitations last more than a few minutes, or happen during a run, stop and see us."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I will. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in three weeks, with the results."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Three weeks. Thanks. ~"
  }
 ],
